  "notes": "As of October 2026, most Minnesota state-licensed and tribal dispensaries are discoverable on Leafly, indicating Leafly is a primary aggregation platform. Specific backend POS systems (Dutchie, BLAZE, Jane, Treez) are not always publicly disclosed by individual dispensaries. Terpene disclosure is optional, creating competitive differentiation. No potency cap on adult-use flower or concentrate is in force; SF 3591 and SF 4434 (2026) proposed one and were not enacted. Seed sources in Minnesota are licensed under the Department of Agriculture, not OCM, allowing non-licensed retailers to sell seeds."
